<!doctype html>
<html lang=\"en\">
<head>
  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />
  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />
  <title>Amazon Bestselling Books: Price vs. User Rating Trend Analysis (2009–2019)</title>
  <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.3/dist/chart.umd.min.js\"></script>
  <style>
    :root{
      --bg:#0b1220;
      --panel:#101b33;
      --panel-2:#0f1930;
      --text:#e9eefc;
      --muted:#b7c3e6;
      --grid:rgba(255,255,255,.08);
      --accent:#69b3ff;
      --accent2:#8ef0c5;
      --warn:#ffb86b;
      --danger:#ff6b6b;
      --nf:#69b3ff;
      --fic:#8ef0c5;
      --shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
      --radius: 14px;
    }
    *{box-sizing:border-box}
    body{
      margin:0;
      font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, \"Apple Color Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Emoji\";
      background: radial-gradient(1200px 900px at 20% 10%, rgba(105,179,255,.14), transparent 60%),
                  radial-gradient(1100px 800px at 90% 30%, rgba(142,240,197,.12), transparent 55%),
                  var(--bg);
      color:var(--text);
      line-height:1.45;
    }
    header{
      padding: 34px 22px 18px;
      max-width: 1200px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    h1{margin:0 0 8px; font-size: 28px; letter-spacing:.2px}
    .subtitle{color:var(--muted); margin:0; max-width: 980px}
    .meta{margin-top:10px; color:var(--muted); font-size:13px}

    main{max-width:1200px; margin:0 auto; padding: 10px 22px 44px;}
    .grid{display:grid; gap:14px;}
    .kpi-grid{grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0,1fr));}
    .two-col{grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .8fr; align-items:start;}
    .three-col{grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr));}

    .card{
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,.03), rgba(255,255,255,.01));
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      padding: 16px 16px;
    }
    .card h2{margin:0 0 10px; font-size:18px}
    .card h3{margin:0 0 8px; font-size:15px; color:var(--text)}

    .kpi{
      padding:14px 14px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.02);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
      min-height: 92px;
    }
    .kpi .label{color:var(--muted); font-size:12px; margin-bottom:6px}
    .kpi .value{font-size:22px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.2px}
    .kpi .note{color:var(--muted); font-size:12px; margin-top:6px}

    .pill{
      display:inline-flex;
      align-items:center;
      gap:8px;
      border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      font-size:12px;
      color: var(--muted);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.02);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .dot{width:10px; height:10px; border-radius:50%}
    .dot.fic{background:var(--fic)}
    .dot.nf{background:var(--nf)}

    .section{margin-top:14px}
    .section-title{display:flex; align-items:flex-end; justify-content:space-between; gap:12px; margin: 10px 2px 10px;}
    .section-title h2{margin:0; font-size:20px}
    .section-title p{margin:0; color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; max-width: 820px}

    .chart-wrap{height: 310px;}
    .chart-wrap.tall{height: 360px;}
    canvas{width:100% !important; height:100% !important;}

    table{width:100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size:13px}
    th, td{padding:10px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08); vertical-align: top;}
    th{color:var(--muted); font-weight:600; text-align:left}
    td{color:var(--text)}
    .num{text-align:right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;}

    .callout{
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      padding: 10px 12px;
      background: rgba(105,179,255,.07);
      border-radius: 12px;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .callout strong{color: var(--text)}

    .bullets{margin:0; padding-left: 18px; color: var(--text)}
    .bullets li{margin: 6px 0; color: var(--text)}
    .muted{color:var(--muted)}

    footer{max-width:1200px; margin:0 auto; padding: 0 22px 28px; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px}

    @media (max-width: 1080px){
      .kpi-grid{grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr));}
      .two-col{grid-template-columns: 1fr;}
      .three-col{grid-template-columns: 1fr;}
      .chart-wrap{height: 290px}
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>Amazon Bestselling Books: Price vs. User Rating Trend Analysis (2009–2019)</h1>
    <p class=\"subtitle\">A management-oriented view of how pricing relates to customer satisfaction, how those dynamics differ by genre, and how both shifted year-over-year across Amazon’s annual Top‑50 bestseller lists (550 entries, 2009–2019).</p>
    <div class=\"meta\">Dataset: 50 bestsellers per year (2009–2019). Unit: USD list price (integer dollars in source). Ratings: 0–5. Reviews: count.</div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class=\"card\">
      <div class=\"section-title\" style=\"margin-top:0\">
        <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
        <p>Key signals management can act on immediately; all values computed directly from <code>data.csv</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid kpi-grid\">
        <div class=\"kpi\"><div class=\"label\">Records (annual bestseller entries)</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"kpiRows\"></div><div class=\"note\" id=\"kpiYears\"></div></div>
        <div class=\"kpi\"><div class=\"label\">Average Price (overall)</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"kpiAvgPrice\"></div><div class=\"note\" id=\"kpiPriceRange\"></div></div>
        <div class=\"kpi\"><div class=\"label\">Average User Rating (overall)</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"kpiAvgRating\"></div><div class=\"note\" id=\"kpiRatingRange\"></div></div>
        <div class=\"kpi\"><div class=\"label\">Average Review Count (overall)</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"kpiAvgReviews\"></div><div class=\"note\" id=\"kpiReviewsRange\"></div></div>
        <div class=\"kpi\"><div class=\"label\">Price–Rating Correlation (Pearson r)</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"kpiCorr\"></div><div class=\"note\">Negative values imply higher price ↔ slightly lower ratings.</div></div>
      </div>

      <div class=\"grid two-col\" style=\"margin-top:14px\">
        <div class=\"callout\">
          <strong>Headline finding:</strong> Across 2009–2019 bestsellers, price and rating show a <strong>weak negative</strong> relationship (Pearson <span id=\"corrInline\"></span>). In practice: higher prices do <em>not</em> buy higher customer satisfaction on the bestseller list—value perception is driven more by content/fit than by price positioning.
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style=\"display:flex; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap\">
            <span class=\"pill\"><span class=\"dot nf\"></span>Non Fiction</span>
            <span class=\"pill\"><span class=\"dot fic\"></span>Fiction</span>
            <span class=\"pill\">Most common price bands: $5–$9, $10–$14</span>
          </div>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Implication: pricing can be optimized for margin/volume without expecting systematic rating lift; focus on genre-appropriate price windows and sustained author/franchise investment for repeat appearances.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>1) Bestseller Market Overview (2009–2019)</h2>
        <p>Dataset-level composition, central tendencies, and where the bestseller list “lives” by price segment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid two-col\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Price Segment Mix (Count of entries)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap\"><canvas id=\"priceBuckets\"></canvas></div>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">These are annual Top‑50 <em>entries</em>, not unique titles; repeat bestsellers are counted each year they appear.</p>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>What management should take away</h3>
          <ul class=\"bullets\" id=\"overviewBullets\"></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>2) Price vs. User Rating: Correlation Analysis</h2>
        <p>Quantifies the price–satisfaction relationship and shows the dispersion (not just averages).</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid two-col\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Scatter: Price vs. Rating (All entries)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap tall\"><canvas id=\"scatterAll\"></canvas></div>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Ratings cluster tightly at the high end (bestsellers). That compresses observable rating variation and mechanically limits correlation magnitude.</p>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Correlation KPIs</h3>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Slice</th><th class=\"num\">Pearson r (Price vs Rating)</th><th>Interpretation</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id=\"corrTable\"></tbody>
          </table>
          <div class=\"callout\" style=\"margin-top:12px; border-left-color: var(--warn); background: rgba(255,184,107,.08)\">
            <strong>Actionable read:</strong> Because the relationship is weak and negative, treat price primarily as a <strong>margin + conversion lever</strong>, not a satisfaction lever. Protect ratings via content quality, format/packaging, and expectation-setting (category norms) rather than premium pricing.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>3) Fiction vs. Non-Fiction: Pricing and Rating Strategies</h2>
        <p>Side-by-side, scannable comparison for fast decisions on genre investment and price windows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid two-col\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Genre KPI Comparison</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Genre</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Entries</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Avg Price</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Avg Rating</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Avg Reviews</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Unique Authors</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id=\"genreTable\"></tbody>
          </table>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Note: “Unique authors” counts distinct author strings in the dataset slice (annual entries).</p>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Interpretation for portfolio strategy</h3>
          <ul class=\"bullets\" id=\"genreBullets\"></ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=\"grid three-col\" style=\"margin-top:14px\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Avg Price by Year (Genre split)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap\"><canvas id=\"linePriceGenre\"></canvas></div>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Avg Rating by Year (Genre split)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap\"><canvas id=\"lineRatingGenre\"></canvas></div>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Avg Reviews by Year (Genre split)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap\"><canvas id=\"lineReviewsGenre\"></canvas></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>4) Year-over-Year Trends in Pricing and Ratings (Most Critical)</h2>
        <p>Identifies inflection years where pricing levels or customer sentiment visibly shifted across the bestseller list.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid two-col\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Trend Lines (Overall)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap tall\"><canvas id=\"trendOverall\"></canvas></div>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Left axis: Avg Price (USD). Right axis: Avg Rating. Reviews shown in a separate chart below to keep scales readable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Inflection Points (data-driven)</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Year (vs prior)</th><th class=\"num\">Δ Avg Price</th><th class=\"num\">Δ Avg Rating</th><th class=\"num\">Δ Avg Reviews</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id=\"inflectionTable\"></tbody>
          </table>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Table shows year-over-year deltas. Largest absolute shifts are highlighted in the narrative below.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=\"grid two-col\" style=\"margin-top:14px\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Review Volume Trend (Overall)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap\"><canvas id=\"trendReviews\"></canvas></div>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Review averages rise sharply after 2011–2012, reflecting broader platform engagement and/or longer-tail accumulation among recurring titles.</p>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Management narrative: what changed, when</h3>
          <ul class=\"bullets\" id=\"trendBullets\"></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>5) Dominant Authors on the Bestseller List</h2>
        <p>Which authors sustain presence, and how their price/rating profiles compare (inputs for franchise investment and frontlist/backlist strategy).</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid two-col\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Top Authors by Bestseller Appearances (2009–2019)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap tall\"><canvas id=\"authorsBar\"></canvas></div>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Author KPI Table (Top 15)</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Author</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Appearances</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Unique Titles</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Avg Price</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Avg Rating</th>
                <th class=\"num\">Avg Reviews</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id=\"authorTable\"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>6) Strategic Recommendations</h2>
        <p>Recommendations grounded strictly in observed data patterns (no speculation).</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"card\">
        <ol id=\"recoList\" style=\"margin:0; padding-left: 18px\"></ol>
        <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Each recommendation includes a traceable quantitative basis in the prior sections.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    Generated on 2026-04-30 (UTC). All statistics computed from <code>/app/benchmark/data.csv</code> (550 rows; Top‑50 per year, 2009–2019).
  </footer>

<script>
  // -----------------------------
