        </div>
        <div>
          <div style=\"display:flex; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap\">
            <span class=\"pill\"><span class=\"dot nf\"></span>Non Fiction</span>
            <span class=\"pill\"><span class=\"dot fic\"></span>Fiction</span>
            <span class=\"pill\">Most common price bands: $5–$9, $10–$14</span>
          </div>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Management implication: optimize price for revenue and conversion; protect satisfaction via positioning, packaging, and content fit rather than premium pricing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>1) Bestseller Market Overview (2009–2019)</h2>
        <p>Where the bestseller list sits by price tier and decade-level benchmarks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid two-col\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Price Segment Mix</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap\"><canvas id=\"priceBuckets\"></canvas></div>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
          <ul class=\"bullets\" id=\"overviewBullets\"></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>2) Price vs. User Rating: Correlation Analysis</h2>
        <p>Pearson correlation coefficient plus a scatter visualization.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid two-col\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Scatter (250-entry deterministic sample)</h3>
          <div class=\"chart-wrap tall\"><canvas id=\"scatterAll\"></canvas></div>
          <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:10px 0 0\">Correlation values are computed on the full dataset; scatter uses a deterministic sample to stay readable and fast.</p>
        </div>
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Correlation KPIs</h3>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Slice</th><th class=\"num\">Pearson r</th><th>Interpretation</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id=\"corrTable\"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=\"section\">
      <div class=\"section-title\">
        <h2>3) Fiction vs. Non-Fiction: Pricing and Rating Strategies</h2>
        <p>Side-by-side comparison for fast executive scanning.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=\"grid two-col\">
        <div class=\"card\">
          <h3>Genre KPI Comparison</h3>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Genre</th><th class=\"num\">Entries</th><th class=\"num\">Avg Price</th><th class=\"num\">Avg Rating</th><th class=\"num\">Avg Reviews</th><th class=\"num\">Unique Authors</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id=\"genreTable\"></tbody>
          </table>
